oot ID changed, and exporter behavior, protected data, OS, and kernel were revalidated afterward. The fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart. The main deficiency is operational hygiene due to substantial abandoned test material in /tmp, including copies of the private sibling file.","limitations":["The tests cover representative plain, quoted, and JSON forms but cannot prove correctness for every conceivable email or auth_token syntax.","The authored baseline and executor integrity checks use different digest algorithms, so integrity is established by matching executor-start, pre-restart, and post-restart MD5 observations rather than a same-algorithm comparison to the authored SHA-256 baseline.","Systemd service-state collection is unsupported on this legacy platform, and the package-health probe invokes an unsupported yum check operation; neither shows an executor-caused regression.","The single-node exporter has no separate long-running service or cluster state to recover; restart recovery evidence therefore concerns node reachability, boot identity, exporter behavior, protected data, and platform state."]}
